# The non-secret half of the `internal-auth` group. The credential itself is in
# internal-auth.secret.env; nothing here is one.

# Comma-separated base64 Ed25519 PUBLIC keys accounts keeps verifying and keeps
# publishing at GET /v1/auth/.well-known/jwks.json, beside the key it signs
# with. They are the outgoing half of a signing-key rotation: credentials signed
# by the retiring key must keep verifying until they expire, and auth-gateway
# verifies by `kid` over the whole published set, so publishing both halves is
# what makes a rotation invisible. Standard or raw-url base64; a malformed entry
# is logged and ignored.
#
# Empty is the steady state — one key, nothing retiring. module/KEY_ROTATION.md
# is the runbook.
#
# It is a public key, so it rides in this value file rather than with the
# credential. It is declared at all because KEY_ROTATION.md has told operators
# to set it while no group declared it: a key no group declares is never
# injected, so the retained key was dropped and the rotation it exists to make
# survivable would instead have stopped every outstanding credential verifying.
JWT_PREVIOUS_PUBLIC_KEYS=
